From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 05:44:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the CPU operating points

Add the operating points of the A55 and A76 clusters in a file of their
own, which a board includes with its CPU regulators, as the other
Allwinner SoCs do.

The speed bin in the eFuse selects the points of a die and their
voltage through opp-supported-hw and opp-microvolt-speed<b>. Bins 4 and
5 are known from our boards; the other bins carry vendor values and are
marked so in the file.

Every voltage is a <target target 1050000> window, so that a second
consumer of a rail, such as the DSU, shares it with the CPUs.
clock-latency-ns is the time a cluster runs off its PLL during a rate
change, measured on two boards and rounded up. The points below 780 MHz
stay as limits for thermal and user caps, as on H6 and H616.

Not covered: the fallback points have not been run under load.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; both clusters stepped
through every operating point of their bin at the bin's voltage, and
the fallback table offered its lower top rates.

Assisted-by: LLM
