+/*
+ * CPU operating points of the Allwinner A733, one table per cluster.
+ *
+ * A board includes this file and sets operating-points-v2 on every CPU,
+ * cpu-supply on the first CPU of each cluster.
+ *
+ * Frequencies are 26 MHz * N (the CPU PLLs run from the 26 MHz crystal).
+ * Which points a die runs, and at which voltage, depends on the speed
+ * bin in its eFuse:
+ *
+ *  - opp-supported-hw: bit b is set when bin b runs the point; the bit
+ *    is the fuse value.
+ *  - opp-microvolt-speed<b>: the voltage of bin b, as <target min max>.
+ *    The maximum is the same on both rails so that a second consumer of
+ *    a rail can share the rail's window with the CPUs.
+ *  - opp-microvolt: the highest voltage over all bins at the point. The
+ *    OPP core uses it if a named column is missing.
+ *
+ * Bins 4 and 5 are the dies this table was measured on, at the PMIC.
+ * The columns of bins 1, 2, 3, 6, 20 and 21, and the bits of those bins
+ * in opp-supported-hw, are vendor values, not measured on our boards;
+ * each run of them is marked. 247 and 494 MHz are not vendor points:
+ * they run at the 800 mV that the vendor runs every bin at 416 MHz.
+ *
+ * Bin 1 is the set that a die with no usable bin gets, see
+ * sun50i-cpufreq-nvmem.c.
+ *
+ * clock-latency-ns is the time a cluster is off its PLL during a rate
+ * change, measured with this clock driver.
+ */
+
